e baby teeth already ready to go. That night, Ari put the tooth beneath his pillow. While he slept, Dad exchanged it for a small coin. In the morning, Ari found the coin in its place. Dad''s exchange explains why the objects were there at different times. The four events begin with losing the tooth and end with discovery.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Ari placed the tooth beneath his pillow"},{"id":"c1","label":"Dad exchanged the tooth for a coin"},{"id":"c2","label":"the loose tooth fell out at breakfast"},{"id":"c3","label":"Ari found the coin in the morning"}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"What happened directly after Ari put the tooth under his pillow?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-happened-directly-after-ari-put-the-tooth-under-his-pillow-f396d248ec.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-happened-directly-after-ari-put-the-tooth-under-his-pillow-f396d248ec.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"ari''s family had a little tradition for a lost tooth. first, his loose tooth fell out during breakfast. it was one of the baby teeth already ready to go. that night, ari put the tooth beneath his pillow. while he slept, dad exchanged it for a small coin. in the morning, ari found the coin in its place. dad''s exchange explains why the objects were there at different times. the four events begin with losing the tooth and end with discovery.","constructClaim":"process_order","sourceItemId":"lp3.sequencing.l2.A.process_order.v4","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/sequencing.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.sequencing.l2.A.process_order.v4","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview"