ed letters are drawn in pencil"},{"id":"c1","label":"the letters are painted along their shapes"},{"id":"c2","label":"the rough wood is smoothed with sandpaper"},{"id":"c3","label":"the hanging hooks are fitted to the back"}],"answer":"c1","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-happens-directly-after-drawing-the-pencil-letters-5db539193c.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.sequencing.l2.A.process_order.v20","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"sequencing","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"What happens directly after drawing the pencil letters?","passage":"A wooden sign needs four preparation steps in this workshop. First, the maker rubs the rough board with sandpaper. A smooth surface is easier to write and paint on. Next, she draws the planned letters lightly in pencil. Those lines guide the brush during the following stage. She then paints the letters along the pencil shapes. The back needs hooks rather than painted letters. Last, she attaches hanging hooks to the back of the board. The hooks allow the prepared sign to hang from a rail.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the planned letters are drawn in pencil"},{"id":"c1","label":"the letters are painted along their shapes"},{"id":"c2","label":"the rough wood is smoothed with sandpaper"},{"id":"c3","label":"the hanging hooks are fitted to the back"}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"What happens directly after drawing the pencil letters?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-happens-directly-after-drawing-the-pencil-letters-5db539193c.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-happens-directly-after-drawing-the-pencil-letters-5db539193