2","label":"records the clear layer above the sand"},{"id":"c3","label":"shakes the sealed bottle until cloudy"}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-does-tessa-do-immediately-after-shaking-the-bottle-a92a6ab3ac.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.sequencing.l2.A.process_order.v21","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"sequencing","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"What does Tessa do immediately after shaking the bottle?","passage":"This classroom bottle already contains water and a little sand. Its lid is tight enough to prevent any leaks. First, Tessa shakes the sealed bottle until the water looks cloudy. Next, she sets it upright on the table. During the third stage, the grains settle towards the bottom. Gravity pulls the heavier sand out of the cloudy mixture. Finally, Tessa records the clear water above the settled layer. The still bottle makes that layer easier to observe. Her recording belongs after settling, not while the grains are moving.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"places it upright on the table"},{"id":"c1","label":"waits while the grains settle down"},{"id":"c2","label":"records the clear layer above the sand"},{"id":"c3","label":"shakes the sealed bottle until cloudy"}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"What does Tessa do immediately after shaking the bottle?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-does-tessa-do-immediately-after-shaking-the-bottle-a92a6ab3ac.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-does-tessa-do-immediately-after-shaking-the-bottle-a92a6ab3ac.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"this classroom bottle already contains water and a little sand. its lid is