onge she had baked first. The cake could not have icing while still raw batter. Each part needed the part beneath it to be ready. Her sister saw only the finished cake, not its earlier stages. The sponge formed the base beneath both kinds of decoration.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"showing the finished cake to her sister","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/showing-the-finished-cake-to-her-sister-e1a93c389f.mp3"},{"id":"c1","label":"baking the sponge for the cake","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/baking-the-sponge-for-the-cake-3ee80658d6.mp3"},{"id":"c2","label":"covering the sponge with icing","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/covering-the-sponge-with-icing-206dfbda64.mp3"},{"id":"c3","label":"placing cherries on the white top","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/placing-cherries-on-the-white-top-1b57a2f008.mp3"}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"listening","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"passage","text":"Noor showed her finished birthday cake to her little sister. The cherries on its top looked bright against the white icing. Just before showing it, Noor had placed those cherries carefully. The icing beneath them had gone on earlier. Under that soft layer was a sponge she had baked first. The cake could not have icing while still raw batter. Each part needed the part beneath it to be ready. Her sister saw only the finished cake, not its earlier stages. The sponge formed the base beneath both kinds of decoration.","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_passage/noor-showed-her-finished-birthday-cake-to-her-little-sister-the-cherries-o-9a79ca383d.mp3"},{"role":"instruction","text":"Which task had Noor completed first?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-task-had-noor-completed-first-836fd90697.mp3"},{"role":"choice","text":"showing the f