cy-mock-v1","skillId":"listen_sequencing","domainId":"listening","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"What happens immediately after the glass is crushed?","passage":"At this recycling plant, used glass follows four main stages. Workers first sort the glass into groups by colour. Keeping colours separate helps control the colour of new glass. A machine then crushes each group into small pieces. Those smaller pieces are easier to heat evenly. Next, a very hot furnace melts the crushed glass. Finally, the liquid glass is shaped into new containers. Hard pieces cannot fill a container mould like flowing glass. The plant keeps each stage in its own marked area.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the pieces are melted in a furnace","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-pieces-are-melted-in-a-furnace-7a1a94b966.mp3"},{"id":"c1","label":"the glass is separated by colour","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-glass-is-separated-by-colour-93423f34b0.mp3"},{"id":"c2","label":"the soft glass becomes new containers","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-soft-glass-becomes-new-containers-dbce58b31b.mp3"},{"id":"c3","label":"the sorted glass is broken into pieces","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-sorted-glass-is-broken-into-pieces-ad435da1de.mp3"}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"listening","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"passage","text":"At this recycling plant, used glass follows four main stages. Workers first sort the glass into groups by colour. Keeping colours separate helps control the colour of new glass. A machine then crushes each group into small pieces. Those smaller pieces are easier to heat evenly. Next, a very hot furnace melts the crushed glass. Finally, the liquid glass is shaped into new containers. Har