mbered stops for the day. Those numbers matched the route they had followed.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the hotel beyond the square","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-hotel-beyond-the-square-ea068ff128.mp3"},{"id":"c1","label":"the castle with its tall towers","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-castle-with-its-tall-towers-5724a119b1.mp3"},{"id":"c2","label":"the harbour with the fishing boats","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-harbour-with-the-fishing-boats-5d61e9311d.mp3"},{"id":"c3","label":"the small shops beside the wall","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-small-shops-beside-the-wall-1bddb9aa1f.mp3"}],"answer":"c2","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"listening","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"passage","text":"The walking tour started at the old town''s stone castle. The guide showed the group its tall gate and towers. After the castle visit, the group walked down to the harbour. Fishing boats filled the water beside the narrow path. Next, everyone visited the little shops by the harbour wall. The shops sold postcards showing both boats and the castle. Finally, the group returned to its hotel beyond the square. The guide''s map used four numbered stops for the day. Those numbers matched the route they had followed.","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_passage/the-walking-tour-started-at-the-old-town-s-stone-castle-the-guide-showed-t-890c0da510.mp3"},{"role":"instruction","text":"Which stop came directly after the castle?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-stop-came-directly-after-the-castle-3a243afc7e.mp3"},{"role":"choice","text":"the hotel beyond the square","value":"the hotel beyond the square","path":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-hotel-beyond-the-square-ea068ff128.mp3","choiceId":"c0"},{"role":"choice","text":"