d was too deep for walking. At the island, the waiting visitor came aboard. Only then did the crew return to the mainland. The boat had an empty passenger seat on the outward crossing. That seat was occupied during the final part of the rescue.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the crew launched from the slipway","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-crew-launched-from-the-slipway-d63a69cb81.mp3"},{"id":"c1","label":"the boat crossed towards the island","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-boat-crossed-towards-the-island-946b3fc1a3.mp3"},{"id":"c2","label":"the boat returned to the mainland","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-boat-returned-to-the-mainland-7e9d8881c9.mp3"},{"id":"c3","label":"the visitor climbed into the boat","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-visitor-climbed-into-the-boat-91d21ac040.mp3"}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"listening","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"passage","text":"The rescue crew had a call from an island. A visitor there needed a safe way back to shore. First, the crew launched its boat from the slipway. Next, it crossed the narrow channel to the island. The water between the island and mainland was too deep for walking. At the island, the waiting visitor came aboard. Only then did the crew return to the mainland. The boat had an empty passenger seat on the outward crossing. That seat was occupied during the final part of the rescue.","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_passage/the-rescue-crew-had-a-call-from-an-island-a-visitor-there-needed-a-safe-wa-18919c543b.mp3"},{"role":"instruction","text":"What happened between launching and taking the visitor aboard?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-happened-between-launching-and-taking-the-visitor-aboard-d7820fcfd9.mp3"},{"role":"choice","text":"th