 children do immediately after marking each shadow?","passage":"The class wanted to compare shadows at different times of day. They placed a stick upright in a pot of sand. Its base stayed in one marked place on the playground. At each visit, a child marked the shadow''s tip with chalk. The group wrote the time beside every new chalk mark. Only after the final visit did they join the marks. Then they could compare both the direction and the length. Moving the pot between visits would have spoiled their comparison.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"moved the pot to a new position","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/moved-the-pot-to-a-new-position-88cbf31559.mp3"},{"id":"c1","label":"connected all the marks into a line","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/connected-all-the-marks-into-a-line-53955abb7d.mp3"},{"id":"c2","label":"removed the stick from its sandy pot","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/removed-the-stick-from-its-sandy-pot-62ecc3e6a7.mp3"},{"id":"c3","label":"recorded when that mark was made","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/recorded-when-that-mark-was-made-2ad80d8499.mp3"}],"answer":"c3","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"listening","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"passage","text":"The class wanted to compare shadows at different times of day. They placed a stick upright in a pot of sand. Its base stayed in one marked place on the playground. At each visit, a child marked the shadow''s tip with chalk. The group wrote the time beside every new chalk mark. Only after the final visit did they join the marks. Then they could compare both the direction and the length. Moving the pot between visits would have spoiled their comparison.","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_passage/the-class-wanted-to-compare-shadows-at-different-times-of-day-they-placed--ea370e3709.mp3"},{