l legs. Rolling it away after use removes that danger. A shallow water dish can help during dry weather. A fence gap must stay clear when neighbours replace old boards.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Loose netting can trap the legs of small animals."},{"id":"c1","label":"People can make gardens safer for visiting hedgehogs."},{"id":"c2","label":"A fence gap lets hedgehogs move between nearby gardens."},{"id":"c3","label":"People should inspect garden fires before lighting them."}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which option best states the main idea?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-option-best-states-the-main-idea-2d1ca4b5e8.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-option-best-states-the-main-idea-2d1ca4b5e8.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"hedgehogs often travel through several gardens while looking for food. a small gap below a fence can let them pass. in autumn, a quiet leaf pile offers a sheltered resting place. people should check garden fires for hidden animals before lighting them. netting left loose on the ground can trap small legs. rolling it away after use removes that danger. a shallow water dish can help during dry weather. a fence gap must stay clear when neighbours replace old boards.","constructClaim":"main_idea_vs_detail","sourceItemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.main_idea_vs_detail.v2","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/main_idea.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.main_idea_vs_detail.v2","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"A fence gap lets hedgehogs move between nea