hich sentence sums up the whole passage best?","passage":"Leo wanted to swim the full length of the pool. He usually stopped halfway because he tried to move too quickly. His coach first helped him practise slow breathing beside the edge. Then they worked on steady kicks over a shorter distance. Leo joined the two skills during each lesson that month. Sometimes he still stopped, but he could see his progress. After six weeks, he touched the far wall without standing up. The coach marked the full length on Leo''s progress sheet.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Leo learned that swimming quickly matters more than breathing steadily."},{"id":"c1","label":"Leo improved separate swimming skills and finally completed a full length."},{"id":"c2","label":"Leo practised slow breathing at the pool edge with his coach."},{"id":"c3","label":"Leo reached the far wall first, then began practising shorter distances."}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which sentence sums up the whole passage best?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-sentence-sums-up-the-whole-passage-best-6b881f6d5d.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-sentence-sums-up-the-whole-passage-best-6b881f6d5d.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"leo wanted to swim the full length of the pool. he usually stopped halfway because he tried to move too quickly. his coach first helped him practise slow breathing beside the edge. then they worked on steady kicks over a shorter distance. leo joined the two skills during each lesson that month. sometimes he still stopped, but he could see his progress. after six weeks, he touched the far wall without standing up. the coach marked the full length on leo''s progress sheet.","constructClaim":"summary_choice","sourceItemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.summary_choice.v1","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/main_idea.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.summary_choice.v1","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Leo practised slow breathing at the pool edge with his coach.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN","Leo reached the far wall first, then began practising shorter distances.":"D-OPPOSITE","Leo learned that swimming quickly matters more than breathing steadily.":"D-TOPIC-ADJACENT"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.summary_choice.v2","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Experts carefully assembled and explained a supported dinosaur display."},{"id":"c1","label":"Visitors watched scientists working behind a glass wall at the museum."},{"id":"c2","label":"Experts used only strong original bones and needed no extra supports."},{"id":"c3","label":"Scientists compared fossils to discover what a dinosaur ate."}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-sentence-sums-up-the-whole-passage-best-6b881f6d5d.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.summary_choice.v2","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which sentence sums up the whole passage best?","passage":"A dinosaur skeleton arrived at the museum in numbered boxes. Scientists checked photographs before deciding where each fossil belonged. Some bones were too fragile to support the weight above them. Metal supports held those pieces safely in their correct positions. Visitors watched through glass as the body slowly took shape. A missing section was replaced with a clearly marked model. After a month, the complete display stood above the visitors. Its labels explained both the real fossils and the added supports.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Experts carefully assembled and explained a supported dinosaur display."},{"id":"c1","label":"Visitors watched scientists working behind a glass wall at the museum."},{"id":"c2","label":"Experts used only strong original bones and needed no extra supports."},{"id":"c3","label":"Scientists compared fossils to discover what a dinosaur ate."}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which sentence sums up the whole passage best?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-sentence-sums-up-the-whole-passage-best-6b881f6d5d.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-sentence-sums-up-the-whole-passage-best-6b881f6d5d.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"a dinosaur skeleton arrived at the museum in numbered boxes. scientists checked photographs before deciding where each fossil belonged. some bones were too fragile to support the weight above them. metal supports held those pieces safely in their correct positions. visitors watched through glass as the body slowly took shape. a missing section was replaced with a clearly marked model. after a month, the complete display stood above the visitors. its labels explained both the real fossils and the added supports.","constructClaim":"summary_choice","sourceItemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.summary_choice.v2","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/main_idea.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.summary_choice.v2","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-