ary supports learning through several different services."},{"id":"c1","label":"Visitors can borrow musical instruments from behind the desk."},{"id":"c2","label":"Staff run computer classes for people needing help online."},{"id":"c3","label":"A map drawer helps walkers plan routes without buying guides."}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-statement-gives-the-main-idea-7161fa4962.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.main_idea_vs_detail.v20","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which statement gives the main idea?","passage":"The town library has shelves of books for different readers. Behind the desk, visitors can also borrow simple musical instruments. A map drawer helps walkers plan routes without buying new guides. Families take puzzles home and return them when finished. Staff run small computer classes for people needing help online. A quiet room gives groups space to learn together. These services are available even to visitors who borrow no books. Last week, a new reader returned a drum and borrowed a map.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"The library supports learning through several different services."},{"id":"c1","label":"Visitors can borrow musical instruments from behind the desk."},{"id":"c2","label":"Staff run computer classes for people needing help online."},{"id":"c3","label":"A map drawer helps walkers plan routes without buying guides."}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which statement gives the main idea?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-statement-gives-the-main-idea-7161fa4962.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio