th staff."},{"id":"c1","label":"Volunteers agreed to put the books away after each lunch session."},{"id":"c2","label":"The editors opened a room before asking pupils what they needed."},{"id":"c3","label":"The newspaper persuaded the school to end all noisy lunchtime games."}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-summary-covers-the-whole-passage-65f9c81dcd.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.summary_choice.v21","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which summary covers the whole passage?","passage":"The student newspaper asked pupils what needed changing at school. Many wanted somewhere quiet to read during the busy lunch break. The editors printed those requests and invited other suggestions too. They checked which spare rooms were safe and available then. A meeting with the headteacher settled how the space would run. Volunteers agreed to put books away after each lunch session. The following month, pupils began using a small former meeting room. Their newspaper later reported how readers and helpers were finding it.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Pupils gathered views and organised a quiet reading space with staff."},{"id":"c1","label":"Volunteers agreed to put the books away after each lunch session."},{"id":"c2","label":"The editors opened a room before asking pupils what they needed."},{"id":"c3","label":"The newspaper persuaded the school to end all noisy lunchtime games."}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which summary covers the whole passage?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-summary-covers-the-whole-passage-65f9c81dcd.mp3"}],