","label":"How to Keep Beetles as Pets"},{"id":"c3","label":"The Hottest Path Through the Woods"}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-title-best-covers-this-whole-passage-35535171b3.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.best_title.v46","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which title best covers this whole passage?","passage":"Under a log, the class found beetles and tiny worms. The ground there felt cooler than the sunny path. Damp leaves covered the soil and gave the creatures shelter. The teacher lifted the log just enough for everyone to look. Pupils drew what they saw without touching the small animals. Afterwards, they put the log back in its original place. This kept the dark, damp home ready for its residents. Next week they would compare it with a sunny patch.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"A Hidden Home Beneath Our Feet"},{"id":"c1","label":"A Drawing Lesson in the Classroom"},{"id":"c2","label":"How to Keep Beetles as Pets"},{"id":"c3","label":"The Hottest Path Through the Woods"}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which title best covers this whole passage?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-title-best-covers-this-whole-passage-35535171b3.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-title-best-covers-this-whole-passage-35535171b3.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"under a log, the class found beetles and tiny worms. the ground there felt cooler than the sunny path. damp leaves covered the soil and gave the creatures shelter. the teacher lifted the log just enough for everyone to look. pupils drew what they saw without touching the small animals. afterwards, they put the log back in its original place. this kept the dark, damp home ready for its residents. next week they would compare it with a sunny patch.","constructClaim":"best_title","sourceItemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.best_title.v46","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/main_idea.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.best_title.v46","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved"},"distractorRationales":{"A Drawing Lesson in the Classroom":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","How to Keep Beetles as Pets":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","The Hottest Path Through the Woods":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.best_title.v47","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Choosing the Loudest Radio in Town"},{"id":"c1","label":"Learning to Make Brand New Toys"},{"id":"c2","label":"Filling the Village Rubbish Bins"},{"id":"c3","label":"Giving Worn Things Another Chance"}],"answer":"c3","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-title-best-fits-all-these-events-0a3b6ab4dc.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.best_title.v47","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which title best fits all these events?","passage":"A broken radio arrived at the village repair table. Its owner expected to throw it away and buy another. A volunteer noticed a loose wire near the speaker. She joined the wire safely, and music played again. At the next table, someone sewed a torn school bag. Nearby, a child replaced a missing wheel on a toy. People shared tools, learned new skills and kept useful things. The event left the rubbish bin almost empty that afternoon.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Choosing the Loudest Radio in Town"},{"id":"c1","label":"Learning to Make Brand New Toys"},{"id":"c2","label":"Filling the Village Rubbish Bins"},{"id":"c3","label":"Giving Worn Things Another Chance"}],"answer":"c3","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which title best fits all these events?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-title-best-fits-all-these-events-0a3b6ab4dc.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-title-best-fits-all-these-events-0a3b6ab4dc.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"a broken radio arrived at the village repair table. its owner expected to throw it away and buy another. a volunteer noticed a loose wire near the speaker. she joined the wire safely, and music played again. at the next table, someone sewed a torn school bag. nearby, a child replaced a missing wheel on a toy. people shared tools, learned new skills and kept useful things. the event left the rubbish bin almost empty that afternoon.","constructClaim":"best_title","sourceItemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.best_title.v47","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/main_idea.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.best_title.v47","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved"},"distractorRationales":{"Choosing the Loudest Radio in Town":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Learning to Make Brand New Toys":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Filling the Village Rubbish Bins":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.C.main_idea_vs_detail.v48","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Old sinks hold the plants in the garden."},{"id":"c1","label":"Wooden seats give people somewhere to rest."},{"id":"c2","label":"A barrel collects water from the shelter."},{"id":"c3","label":"Old materials can serve new purposes."}],"answer":"c3","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-idea-connects-the-details-in-this-passage-d5ffc3439e.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.C.main_idea_vs_detail.v48","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which idea connects the details in this passage?","passage":"Our town has a small garden beside the bus station. Herbs grow in old sinks that would otherwise be thrown away. A rain barrel catches water from the roof of the shelter. Fallen leaves become compost in a corner bin. Volunteers use the compost to feed next year''s plants. Wooden pallets form seats where people can rest and talk. Labels explain what each reused object used to be. The garden shows how unwanted materials can become useful again.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Old sinks hold the plants in the garden."},{"id":"c1","label":"Wooden seats give people somewhere to rest."},{"id":"c2","label":"A barrel collects water from the shelter."},{"id":"c3","label":"Old materials can serve new purposes."}],"answer":"c3","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which idea connects the details in this passage?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-idea-connects-the-details-in-this-passage-d5ffc3439e.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-idea-connects-the-details-in-this-passage-d5ffc3439e.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"our town has a small garden beside the bus station. herbs grow in old sinks that would otherwise be thrown away. a rain barrel catches water from the roof of the shelter. fallen leaves become compost in a corner bin. volunteers use the compost to feed next year''s plants. wooden pallets form seats where people can rest and talk. labels explain what each reused object used to be. the garden shows how unwanted materials can become useful again.","constructClaim":"main_idea_vs_detail","sourceItemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.C.main_idea_vs_detail.v48","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/main_idea.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.C.main_idea_vs_detail.v48","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved"},"distractorRationales":{"Old sinks hold the plants in the garden.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN","Wooden seats give people somewhere to rest.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN","A barrel collects water from the shelter.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.main_idea_vs_detail.v49","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Birds are the only danger near a shore."},{"id":"c1","label":"Pool animals protect themselves in different ways."},{"id":"c2","label":"Only crabs can hide from larger animals."},{"id":"c3","label":"All sea creatures are safe beneath the water."}],"answer":"c1","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-idea-is-supported-by-the-whole-passage-346e6a808e.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.main_idea_vs_detail.v49","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which idea is supported by the whole passage?","passage":"The rock pool looked still, but many creatures lived there. A crab hid beneath a ledge until a bird''s shadow passed. A limpet held tightly to the rock as waves splashed over. Small fish darted between strands of seaweed to escape a bird. Each animal used a different way to stay safe. The class watched from the edge and kept their hands out. They recorded the shelter or action each creature used. Their notes showed several solutions to the same problem.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Birds are the only danger near a shore."},{"id":"c1","label":"Pool animals protect themselves in different ways."},{"id":"c2","label":"Only crabs can hide from larger animals."},{"id":"c3","label":"All sea creatures are safe beneath the water."}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which idea is supported by the whole passage?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-idea-is-supported-by-the-whole-passage-346e6a808e.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-idea-is-supported-by-the-whole-passage-346e6a808e.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"the rock pool looked still, but many creatures lived there. a crab hid beneath a ledge until a bird''s shadow passed. a limpet held tightly to the rock as waves splashed over. small fish darted between strands of seaweed to escape a bird. each animal used a different way to stay safe. the class watched from the edge and kept their hands out. they recorded the shelter or action each creature used. their notes showed several solutions to the same problem.","constructClaim":"main_idea_vs_detail","sourceItemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.main_idea_vs_detail.v49","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/main_idea.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.A.main_idea_vs_detail.v49","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved"},"distractorRationales":{"Only crabs can hide from larger animals.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","All sea creatures are safe beneath the water.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Birds are the only danger near a shore.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.summary_choice.v50","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"They tested a problem and improved how the plants received water."},{"id":"c1","label":"They planted new vegetables because every old plant had already died."},{"id":"c2","label":"They counted buckets and decided the garden needed a longer path."},{"id":"c3","label":"They covered the whole garden and stopped watering during warm weather."}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-sentence-best-summarises-what-the-group-did-0d069ccd27.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.summary_choice.v50","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"main_idea","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which sentence best summarises what the group did?","passage":"The school''s vegetable bed was too dry during a warm week. A group measured how much water each row received. They found most water ran off the hard surface. They loosened the soil and spread straw around the plants. Then they watered slowly instead of emptying a full bucket. More water soaked in, and less escaped down the path. The leaves looked firmer the next morning. The group wrote down the changes so other classes could use them.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"They tested a problem and improved how the plants received water."},{"id":"c1","label":"They planted new vegetables because every old plant had already died."},{"id":"c2","label":"They counted buckets and decided the garden needed a longer path."},{"id":"c3","label":"They covered the whole garden and stopped watering during warm weather."}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which sentence best summarises what the group did?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-sentence-best-summarises-what-the-group-did-0d069ccd27.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-sentence-best-summarises-what-the-group-did-0d069ccd27.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"the school''s vegetable bed was too dry during a warm week. a group measured how much water each row received. they found most water ran off the hard surface. they loosened the soil and spread straw around the plants. then they watered slowly instead of emptying a full bucket. more water soaked in, and less escaped down the path. the leaves looked firmer the next morning. the group wrote down the changes so other classes could use them.","constructClaim":"summary_choice","sourceItemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.summary_choice.v50","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/main_idea.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.main_idea.l2.B.summary_choice.v50","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved"},"distractorRationales":{"They planted new vegetables because every old plant had already died.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","They counted buckets and decided the garden needed a longer path.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","They covered the whole garden and stopped watering during warm weather.":"D-