g","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which title fits this passage best?","passage":"Asha wanted to play a fast rhythm at the concert. Each evening, her sticks missed the same beats halfway through. She tried hitting harder, but the mistake stayed the same. Her teacher asked her to play each part very slowly. Asha disliked how plain the slow rhythm sounded at first. Soon she could hear exactly where her hands lost time. She joined the parts, then carefully increased her speed. At the concert, she played the whole rhythm without stumbling.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Choosing an Easier Tune for the Concert","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/choosing-an-easier-tune-for-the-concert-9d90527480.mp3"},{"id":"c1","label":"Slowing Down to Master a Fast Rhythm","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/slowing-down-to-master-a-fast-rhythm-1cbfe72971.mp3"},{"id":"c2","label":"Practicing the Middle Beats of a Tune","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/practicing-the-middle-beats-of-a-tune-0a3691b883.mp3"},{"id":"c3","label":"Making Drums Louder for a Large Audience","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/making-drums-louder-for-a-large-audience-cbdafbf6ca.mp3"}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"listening","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"passage","text":"Asha wanted to play a fast rhythm at the concert. Each evening, her sticks missed the same beats halfway through. She tried hitting harder, but the mistake stayed the same. Her teacher asked her to play each part very slowly. Asha disliked how plain the slow rhythm sounded at first. Soon she could hear exactly where her hands lost time. She joined the parts, then carefully increased her speed. At the concert, she played the whole rhythm without stumbling.","path":"/audio/productio