omainId":"listening","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which title best covers this whole passage?","passage":"Under a log, the class found beetles and tiny worms. The ground there felt cooler than the sunny path. Damp leaves covered the soil and gave the creatures shelter. The teacher lifted the log just enough for everyone to look. Pupils drew what they saw without touching the small animals. Afterwards, they put the log back in its original place. This kept the dark, damp home ready for its residents. Next week they would compare it with a sunny patch.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"A Hidden Home Beneath Our Feet","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/a-hidden-home-beneath-our-feet-fbb35e374c.mp3"},{"id":"c1","label":"A Drawing Lesson in the Classroom","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/a-drawing-lesson-in-the-classroom-46675e9ee7.mp3"},{"id":"c2","label":"How to Keep Beetles as Pets","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/how-to-keep-beetles-as-pets-0f623a71a0.mp3"},{"id":"c3","label":"The Hottest Path Through the Woods","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-hottest-path-through-the-woods-8e80694f4a.mp3"}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"listening","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"passage","text":"Under a log, the class found beetles and tiny worms. The ground there felt cooler than the sunny path. Damp leaves covered the soil and gave the creatures shelter. The teacher lifted the log just enough for everyone to look. Pupils drew what they saw without touching the small animals. Afterwards, they put the log back in its original place. This kept the dark, damp home ready for its residents. Next week they would compare it with a sunny patch.","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_passage/under-a-log-the-class