 was working next door"},{"id":"c3","label":"the blender made a lot of noise"}],"answer":"c2","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which reason for missing the call is NOT given?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-reason-for-missing-the-call-is-not-given-a6d74cf41c.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-reason-for-missing-the-call-is-not-given-a6d74cf41c.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"the phone rang while the family made lunch. a loud blender mixed a drink. the radio played music at full volume. cushions also covered the phone, making its sound quieter. nobody heard it above the other noises. the phone lay on the sofa near the kitchen doorway. its screen lit up under a fold in the cloth. sound from the kitchen reached the sofa much more loudly. the missed-call mark remained there after the music and blender stopped.","constructClaim":"multiple_causes","sourceItemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.multiple_causes.v7","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/cause_effect.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.multiple_causes.v7","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"the radio was playing very loudly":"D-SUPPORTED-DETAIL","cushions made the phone sound quieter":"D-SUPPORTED-DETAIL","the blender made a lot of noise":"D-SUPPORTED-DETAIL"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.multiple_causes.v8","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the rowers had tired arms from swimming"},{"id":"c1","label":"water leaked into the bottom of the boat"},{"id":"c2","label":"the tide moved against the little boat"},{"id":"c3","label":"wind pushed back against the little boat"}],"answer":"c1","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-reason-for-slow-rowing-is-not-given-5963026f5c.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.multiple_causes.v8","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which reason for slow rowing is NOT given?","passage":"Rowing home was hard that afternoon. The tide moved against the little boat. Wind from the shore pushed against it too. Both rowers had tired arms after a long swim. They rested before trying the last part of the trip. Each pull moved the oars through water pushing the other way. The breeze acted on the boat above the water as well. Their muscles had already worked hard before the return journey. Together, these difficulties explain why their progress was so slow.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the rowers had tired arms from swimming"},{"id":"c1","label":"water leaked into the bottom of the boat"},{"id":"c2","label":"the tide moved against the little boat"},{"id":"c3","label":"wind pushed back against the little boat"}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which reason for slow rowing is NOT given?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-reason-for-slow-rowing-is-not-given-5963026f5c.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-reason-for-slow-rowing-is-not-given-5963026f5c.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"rowing home was hard that afternoon. the tide moved against the little boat. wind from the shore pushed against it too. both rowers had tired arms after a long swim. they rested before trying the last part of the trip. each pull moved the oars through water pushing the other way. the breeze acted on the boat above the water as well. their muscles had already worked hard before the return journey. together, these difficulties explain why their progress was so slow.","constructClaim":"multiple_causes","sourceItemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.multiple_causes.v8","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/cause_effect.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.multiple_causes.v8","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"the tide moved against the little boat":"D-SUPPORTED-DETAIL","wind pushed back against the little boat":"D-SUPPORTED-DETAIL","the rowers had tired arms from swimming":"D-SUPPORTED-DETAIL"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v1","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the cat followed the children''s choice"},{"id":"c1","label":"the teacher chose a place for both"},{"id":"c2","label":"the visitor called the cat to them"},{"id":"c3","label":"the children followed the cat''s choice"}],"answer":"c3","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-caused-the-children-and-the-cat-to-gather-in-the-same-place-26e54a8036.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v1","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"What caused the children and the cat to gather in the same place?","passage":"Children often gathered wherever the school cat sat. A visitor thought their voices called the cat over. The teacher watched more carefully. The cat chose a sunny place first. Only then did children walk over to sit nearby. On one morning, the children were inside until a late break. The cat was already stretched out beside the warm wall. When a cloud shaded that patch, it moved to another corner. Children joined it there only after they came out for playtime.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the cat followed the children''s choice"},{"id":"c1","label":"the teacher chose a place for both"},{"id":"c2","label":"the visitor called the cat to them"},{"id":"c3","label":"the children followed the cat''s choice"}],"answer":"c3","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"What caused the children and the cat to gather in the same place?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-caused-the-children-and-the-cat-to-gather-in-the-same-place-26e54a8036.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/what-caused-the-children-and-the-cat-to-gather-in-the-same-place-26e54a8036.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"children often gathered wherever the school cat sat. a visitor thought their voices called the cat over. the teacher watched more carefully. the cat chose a sunny place first. only then did children walk over to sit nearby. on one morning, the children were inside until a late break. the cat was already stretched out beside the warm wall. when a cloud shaded that patch, it moved to another corner. children joined it there only after they came out for playtime.","constructClaim":"reversal_trap","sourceItemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v1","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/cause_effect.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v1","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"the visitor called the cat to them":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","the cat followed the children''s choice":"D-CAUSE-REVERSE","the teacher chose a place for both":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.reversal_trap.v2","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the prizes she received after racing"},{"id":"c1","label":"the cheering she heard after winning"},{"id":"c2","label":"the training she had done regularly"},{"id":"c3","label":"the red socks she wore that day"}],"answer":"c2","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/what-does-the-passage-suggest-really-made-jo-fast-09fe2eff56.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.reversal_trap.v2","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"What does the passage suggest REALLY made Jo fast?","passage":"Jo won three races while wearing her red socks. She said the socks had made her faster. Her coach showed her the training chart from two months. She had practiced on every marked day. The coach said that work had made her faster. The chart also showed her practice times getting shorter each week. Some of those quicker runs happened in plain white socks. Her first prize came after the improvement was already recorded. The rewards followed her speed; they could not explain the earlier progress.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the prizes she received after racing"},{"id":"c1","label":"the cheering she heard after winning"},{"id":"c2","label":"the training she had done regularly"},{"id":"c3","label":"the red socks she wore that day"}],"answer":"c2","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"im