ng the cupboard reminded Dad to get dinner"},{"id":"c3","label":"Dad fetching dinner made Biscuit come into the kitchen"}],"answer":"c3","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-explanation-fits-the-order-and-cause-described-25133012ee.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.C.reversal_trap.v3","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which explanation fits the order and cause described?","passage":"Dad stepped on a creaky board while fetching Biscuit''s meal. Hearing that familiar noise, the dog came into the kitchen. A visitor thought Dad fetched food because Biscuit had arrived. But Dad had started before the dog left its bed. The clock showed the dog''s usual feeding time. Dad followed that time even when Biscuit was asleep. His footsteps made the sound that drew the dog closer. The visitor had noticed the response without seeing its earlier trigger.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Biscuit entering the kitchen made Dad start fetching dinner"},{"id":"c1","label":"the visitor asking for dinner made Dad fetch dog food"},{"id":"c2","label":"Biscuit scratching the cupboard reminded Dad to get dinner"},{"id":"c3","label":"Dad fetching dinner made Biscuit come into the kitchen"}],"answer":"c3","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which explanation fits the order and cause described?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-explanation-fits-the-order-and-cause-described-25133012ee.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-explanation-fits-the-order-and-cause-described-25133012ee.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"dad stepped on a creaky board while fetching biscuit''s meal. hearing that familiar noise, the dog came into the kitchen. a visitor thought dad fetched food because biscuit had arrived. but dad had started before the dog left its bed. the clock showed the dog''s usual feeding time. dad followed that time even when biscuit was asleep. his footsteps made the sound that drew the dog closer. the visitor had noticed the response without seeing its earlier trigger.","constructClaim":"reversal_trap","sourceItemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.C.reversal_trap.v3","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/cause_effect.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.C.reversal_trap.v3","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Biscuit scratching the cupboard reminded Dad to get dinner":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Biscuit entering the kitchen made Dad start fetching dinner":"D-CAUSE-REVERSE","the visitor asking for dinner made Dad fetch dog food":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v4","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"each group responded by becoming louder in turn"},{"id":"c1","label":"the band’s first response caused the earlier crowd singing"},{"id":"c2","label":"the louder crowd stopped the band from playing loudly"},{"id":"c3","label":"the louder band stopped the crowd from singing loudly"}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/what-does-the-passage-say-about-the-noise-286cfad59b.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v4","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"What does the passage say about the noise?","passage":"The crowd sang loudly, encouraging the band to play harder. Hearing the louder band, the crowd sang even louder. The band responded by playing harder again. Both groups kept encouraging each other through the final song. The extra volume did not start with both groups at once. At the first chorus, the audience''s strong singing changed the playing. During the next chorus, that stronger playing changed the singing. Looking at only one chorus would miss part of the whole pattern.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"each group responded by becoming louder in turn"},{"id":"c1","label":"the band’s first response caused the earlier crowd singing"},{"id":"c2","label":"the louder crowd stopped the band from playing loudly"},{"id":"c3","label":"the louder band stopped the crowd from singing loudly"}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"What does the passage say about the noise?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/what-does-the-passage-say-about-the-noise-286cfad59b.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/what-does-the-passage-say-about-the-noise-286cfad59b.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"the crowd sang loudly, encouraging the band to play harder. hearing the louder band, the crowd sang even louder. the band responded by playing harder again. both groups kept encouraging each other through the final song. the extra volume did not start with both groups at once. at the first chorus, the audience''s strong singing changed the playing. during the next chorus, that stronger playing changed the singing. looking at only one chorus would miss part of the whole pattern.","constructClaim":"reversal_trap","sourceItemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v4","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/cause_effect.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v4","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"the band’s first response caused the earlier crowd singing":"D-CAUSE-REVERSE","the louder crowd stopped the band from playing loudly":"D-OPPOSITE","the louder band stopped the crowd from singing loudly":"D-OPPOSITE"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.reversal_trap.v5","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"opening umbrellas made the rain begin"},{"id":"c1","label":"people opened umbrellas to bring cooler air"},{"id":"c2","label":"opening umbrellas made the rain stop"},{"id":"c3","label":"the rain made people open umbrellas"}],"answer":"c3","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/why-do-umbrellas-and-rain-arrive-together-8e94388d54.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.reversal_trap.v5","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Why do umbrellas and rain arrive together?","passage":"Umbrellas opened all along the street as rain began. It might look as if opening umbrellas brought the rain. But the first drops landed before any umbrella opened. People opened them to keep those drops off their clothes. One person without an umbrella sheltered beneath a shop roof. Another person waited indoors until the shower became lighter. The drops reached the street in places with no people too. The weather affected the people wherever they chose to shelter.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"opening umbrellas made the rain begin"},{"id":"c1","label":"people opened umbrellas to bring cooler air"},{"id":"c2","label":"opening umbrellas made the rain stop"},{"id":"c3","label":"the rain made people open umbrellas"}],"answer":"c3","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Why do umbrellas and rain arrive together?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/why-do-umbrellas-and-rain-arrive-together-8e94388d54.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/why-do-umbrellas-and-rain-arrive-together-8e94388d54.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"umbrellas opened all along the street as rain began. it might look as if opening umbrellas brought the rain. but the first drops landed before any umbrella opened. people opened them to keep those drops off their clothes. one person without an umbrella sheltered beneath a shop roof. another person waited indoors until the shower became lighter. the drops reached the street in places with no people too. the weather affected the people wherever they chose to shelter.","constructClaim":"reversal_trap","sourceItemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.reversal_trap.v5","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/cause_effect.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.B.reversal_trap.v5","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"opening umbrellas made the rain begin":"D-CAUSE-REVERSE","people opened umbrellas to bring cooler air":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","opening umbrellas made the rain stop":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.C.reversal_trap.v6","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"a long gap since lunch made him hungry"},{"id":"c1","label":"the truck''s music always made him hungry"},{"id":"c2","label":"hearing Mom''s question made him need food"},{"id":"c3","label":"buying ice cream made the truck arrive"}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/what-really-explains-tam-s-four-o-clock-hunger-e58659f224.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.C.reversal_trap.v6","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"What REALLY explains Tam''s four o''clock hunger?","passage":"Tam felt hungry when the ice cream music played. He thought the tune caused his hunger. Mom asked him to notice days without the truck. He was hungry at four on those days too. Lunch was early, and his body needed food again. The truck followed its route even when nobody bought a cone. Tam noticed his empty stomach before hearing it on Tuesday. On Wednesday, the truck never came down their road. He still wanted his usual afternoon snack at about the same time.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"a long gap since lunch made him hungry"},{"id":"c1","label":"the truck''s music always made him hungry"},{"id":"c2","label":"hearing Mom''s question made him need food"},{"id":"c3","label":"buying ice cream made the truck arrive"}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"What REALLY explains Tam''s four o''clock hunger?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/what-really-explains-tam-s-four-o-clock-hunger-e58659f224.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/what-really-explains-tam-s-four-o-clock-hunger-e58659f224.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"tam felt hungry when the ice cream music played. he thought the