ghten. The farmer joked that its crow had lifted the sun. But dawn came on quiet mornings too. The rooster noticed the early light and began crowing. The bird''s coop had a window facing the lightening sky. The farmer could see daylight there before hearing the first call. A recording of yesterday''s crow played at noon changed nothing outside. The passage describes this bird responding to dawn, not controlling the time.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the fading daylight made the rooster call"},{"id":"c1","label":"the brightening sky prompted the bird’s call"},{"id":"c2","label":"the rooster’s crow brought the morning light"},{"id":"c3","label":"the farmer’s joke made the sky grow bright"}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which explanation does the passage support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-explanation-does-the-passage-support-70f416ce6b.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-explanation-does-the-passage-support-70f416ce6b.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"a rooster crowed as the sky began to brighten. the farmer joked that its crow had lifted the sun. but dawn came on quiet mornings too. the rooster noticed the early light and began crowing. the bird''s coop had a window facing the lightening sky. the farmer could see daylight there before hearing the first call. a recording of yesterday''s crow played at noon changed nothing outside. the passage describes this bird responding to dawn, not controlling the time.","constructClaim":"reversal_trap","sourceItemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v7","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/cause_effect.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.c