howed yesterday''s delivery date. checking these details separated two mistakes from two things done properly.","constructClaim":"multiple_causes","sourceItemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.multiple_causes.v20","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/cause_effect.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.multiple_causes.v20","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved"},"distractorRationales":{"both the early opening and missing flour":"D-SUPPORTED-DETAIL","the oven door opened before it should":"D-SUPPORTED-DETAIL","the mixture contained too little flour":"D-SUPPORTED-DETAIL"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v20","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the heater’s warmth caused the ice to melt"},{"id":"c1","label":"the melting ice caused the heater to switch on"},{"id":"c2","label":"the solid ice caused the room to become warmer"},{"id":"c3","label":"switching off the heater caused faster melting"}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-cause-and-effect-fits-the-evidence-7e92ed8fec.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v20","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"cause_effect","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which cause and effect fits the evidence?","passage":"The heater warmed the room, and then the ice sculpture melted. Turning the heater off slowed the melting. The sculpture had stayed solid before the room became warm. The display stood well away from the switch on the wall. Staff recorded the room temperature beside a picture of the sculpture. The temperature rose before the first drop appeared under the base. At the cooler setting, drops formed less quickly. The order and the changed setting supported the same explanation.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"the heater’s warmth caused the ice to melt"},{"id":"c1","label":"the melting ice caused the heater to switch on"},{"id":"c2","label":"the solid ice caused the room to become warmer"},{"id":"c3","label":"switching off the heater caused faster melting"}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which cause and effect fits the evidence?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-cause-and-effect-fits-the-evidence-7e92ed8fec.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-cause-and-effect-fits-the-evidence-7e92ed8fec.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"the heater warmed the room, and then the ice sculpture melted. turning the heater off slowed the melting. the sculpture had stayed solid before the room became warm. the display stood well away from the switch on the wall. staff recorded the room temperature beside a picture of the sculpture. the temperature rose before the first drop appeared under the base. at the cooler setting, drops formed less quickly. the order and the changed setting supported the same explanation.","constructClaim":"reversal_trap","sourceItemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v20","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/cause_effect.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.cause_effect.l2.A.reversal_trap.v20","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved"},"distractorRationales":{"the solid ice caused the room to become warmer":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","switching off the heater caused fas