r-indoors-fc7e4913da.mp3"},{"id":"c1","label":"children spent too much time outside","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/children-spent-too-much-time-outside-6bac3383f2.mp3"},{"id":"c2","label":"children with colds came into school","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/children-with-colds-came-into-school-1f2b3f19f0.mp3"},{"id":"c3","label":"children crowded together in one room","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/children-crowded-together-in-one-room-b7526d95d2.mp3"}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"listening","displayPassageDuringResponse":false,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"passage","text":"Several children had colds when they came to school. Rain kept the class crowded indoors all week. The windows stayed shut, so little fresh air came inside. Germs could spread easily in the crowded room. By Friday, more children had colds. The room had enough seats but little space between groups. Children shared the same indoor air throughout each wet day. An open window would have helped replace that air. These conditions helped germs pass between children sharing the room.","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_passage/several-children-had-colds-when-they-came-to-school-rain-kept-the-class-cr-c0cf56472b.mp3"},{"role":"instruction","text":"Which reason for spreading colds is NOT given?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-reason-for-spreading-colds-is-not-given-7945bff1cc.mp3"},{"role":"choice","text":"children had little fresh air indoors","value":"children had little fresh air indoors","path":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/children-had-little-fresh-air-indoors-fc7e4913da.mp3","choiceId":"c0"},{"role":"choice","text":"children spent too much time outside","value":"children spent too much time outside","path":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/children-spent-too-much-time-outside-6bac3383f