 a slow walk beside the river. He stopped often to look at birds or talk with neighbours. His pace on school mornings was brisk instead. Ida needed several quick steps to match each of his strides. They still used the same smooth path beside the river. Dad did not stumble or walk quietly on his toes. He moved with purpose, reaching the gate before the bell. On the return journey, he slowed down and watched the ducks again.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Quiet so that nobody could hear footsteps.","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/quiet-so-that-nobody-could-hear-footsteps-1b9fcf1156.mp3"},{"id":"c1","label":"Quick and full of purposeful energy.","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/quick-and-full-of-purposeful-energy-8cd9c388f1.mp3"},{"id":"c2","label":"Slow and relaxed with frequent stops.","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/slow-and-relaxed-with-frequent-stops-609922693d.mp3"},{"id":"c3","label":"Unsteady because the path was uneven.","audioPath":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/unsteady-because-the-path-was-uneven-4b19eddf40.mp3"}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"brisk","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"brisk","modality":"recognition","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"In this passage, what does \"brisk\" mean?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/in-this-passage-what-does-brisk-mean-aaa8a17aed.mp3"},{"role":"target_word","text":"brisk","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/brisk-3b85777af1.mp3"},{"role":"choice","text":"Quiet so that nobody could hear footsteps.","value":"Quiet so that nobody could hear footsteps.","path":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/quiet-so-that-nobody-could-hear-footsteps-1b9fcf1156.mp3","choiceId":"c0"},{"role":"choice","text":"Quick and full of purposeful energy.","value":"Quick and full of purposeful energy.","path":"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/