qual turns can settle a disagreement."},{"id":"c2","label":"Strict punishment is needed before children will consider their neighbours."},{"id":"c3","label":"Avoiding complaints requires giving up the activity completely."}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which lesson is best supported by the story?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-lesson-is-best-supported-by-the-story-65e6826fff.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-lesson-is-best-supported-by-the-story-65e6826fff.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"kofi bounced a ball in the stairwell after the rain stopped. the echoes were exciting, and he had not noticed the nearby door. mrs adjei opened it and spoke to him quietly. she explained that a baby inside had just fallen asleep. kofi lowered the ball when he understood who could hear it. she showed him a dry outdoor space with room for bouncing. he moved his game there and invited two friends to join. next day, he checked the stairwell door before deciding where to play.","constructClaim":"theme_among_rivals","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_among_rivals.v7","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_among_rivals.v7","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Strict punishment is needed before children will consider their neighbours.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Avoiding complaints requires giving up the activity completely.":"D-OPPOSITE","Sharing space through equal turns can settle a disagreement.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_among_rivals.v8","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Only people who agree with you deserve help with their plans."},{"id":"c1","label":"Respecting a group’s choice can leave room for later disagreement."},{"id":"c2","label":"Changing an unsuccessful plan can help a group finish its work."},{"id":"c3","label":"Showing disappointment is enough to make other people change a vote."}],"answer":"c1","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-lesson-is-best-supported-by-the-story-65e6826fff.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_among_rivals.v8","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which lesson is best supported by the story?","passage":"Robin wanted the class fund spent on new goal nets. Most classmates voted for a party, so that plan went ahead. Robin felt disappointed but helped serve food and joined the games. Afterwards, he checked the old nets and photographed their torn places. At the next meeting, he explained why they still needed replacing. He waited while others asked questions instead of interrupting their answers. Classmates listened carefully and agreed to save for repairs next. Robin helped list costs beside children who had voted differently before.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Only people who agree with you deserve help with their plans."},{"id":"c1","label":"Respecting a group’s choice can leave room for later disagreement."},{"id":"c2","label":"Changing an unsuccessful plan can help a group finish its work."},{"id":"c3","label":"Showing disappointment is enough to make other people change a vote."}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which lesson is best supported by the story?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-lesson-is-best-supported-by-the-story-65e6826fff.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-lesson-is-best-supported-by-the-story-65e6826fff.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"robin wanted the class fund spent on new goal nets. most classmates voted for a party, so that plan went ahead. robin felt disappointed but helped serve food and joined the games. afterwards, he checked the old nets and photographed their torn places. at the next meeting, he explained why they still needed replacing. he waited while others asked questions instead of interrupting their answers. classmates listened carefully and agreed to save for repairs next. robin helped list costs beside children who had voted differently before.","constructClaim":"theme_among_rivals","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_among_rivals.v8","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_among_rivals.v8","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Showing disappointment is enough to make other people change a vote.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Only people who agree with you deserve help with their plans.":"D-OPPOSITE","Changing an unsuccessful plan can help a group finish its work.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Sana invited neighbours to look through her telescope during comet week."},{"id":"c1","label":"Sharing an experience can add to what you gain from it."},{"id":"c2","label":"Keeping equipment carefully stored can prevent damage and disappointment."},{"id":"c3","label":"Studying a subject alone can help you become its best expert."}],"answer":"c1","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v1","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which message does the whole story support?","passage":"Sana usually watched the stars alone through her new telescope. She worried that waiting for neighbours would reduce her own viewing time. During comet week, a child nearby asked for a quick look. Sana agreed, then invited the child''s family to take turns. One person noticed a pale tail she had missed herself. Another shared a drawing showing where the comet had moved. Sana spent less time at the eyepiece but talked excitedly for longer. She left an invitation beside the telescope for the following evening.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Sana invited neighbours to look through her telescope during comet week."},{"id":"c1","label":"Sharing an experience can add to what you gain from it."},{"id":"c2","label":"Keeping equipment carefully stored can prevent damage and disappointment."},{"id":"c3","label":"Studying a subject alone can help you become its best expert."}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which message does the whole story support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"sana usually watched the stars alone through her new telescope. she worried that waiting for neighbours would reduce her own viewing time. during comet week, a child nearby asked for a quick look. sana agreed, then invited the child''s family to take turns. one person noticed a pale tail she had missed herself. another shared a drawing showing where the comet had moved. sana spent less time at the eyepiece but talked excitedly for longer. she left an invitation beside the telescope for the following evening.","constructClaim":"theme_vs_plot","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v1","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v1","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Sana invited neighbours to look through her telescope during comet week.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN","Keeping equipment carefully stored can prevent damage and disappointment.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Studying a subject alone can help you become its best expert.":"D-TOPIC-ADJACENT"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_vs_plot.v2","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Sharing a family story can bring distant relatives together."},{"id":"c1","label":"Marisol visited a small museum after leaving the bus too early."},{"id":"c2","label":"An unexpected change can lead to a worthwhile discovery."},{"id":"c3","label":"Checking directions carefully can prevent a wasted journey."}],"answer":"c2","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_vs_plot.v2","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which message does the whole story support?","passage":"Marisol got off the bus one stop before her intended destination. Rain began while she checked how far she would need to walk. A small museum nearby offered somewhere dry until the shower passed. She expected to wait near the entrance without looking around. A display of old ship models caught her attention instead. She asked the guide about a tiny boat from her grandparents'' town. The rain stopped, but she stayed until the tour had finished. Next week, she returned deliberately with questions for the same guide.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Sharing a family story can bring distant relatives together."},{"id":"c1","label":"Marisol visited a small museum after leaving the bus too early."},{"id":"c2","label":"An unexpected change can lead to a worthwhile discovery."},{"id":"c3","label":"Checking directions carefully can prevent a wasted journey."}],"answer":"c2","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which message does the whole story support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"marisol got off the bus one stop before her intended destination. rain began while she checked how far she would