":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which message does the whole story support?","passage":"Tom swung his bag inside and knocked Grandma''s teapot from its stand. The handle broke, and he first hoped she would not notice. Then he called her and described exactly what had happened. He offered his saved coins towards a repair instead of leaving immediately. Grandma arranged for a repairer to mend the special pot safely. Tom helped pack the pieces and carried the box beside her. Afterwards, he moved his bag hook away from the display shelf. Grandma put the repaired pot back while he hung his bag carefully.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Family stories can make a familiar object feel more special."},{"id":"c1","label":"Tom helped pack the broken teapot before visiting the repairer."},{"id":"c2","label":"Taking responsibility means acting to repair and prevent harm."},{"id":"c3","label":"A precious object should be replaced as soon as it grows old."}],"answer":"c2","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which message does the whole story support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"tom swung his bag inside and knocked grandma''s teapot from its stand. the handle broke, and he first hoped she would not notice. then he called her and described exactly what had happened. he offered his saved coins towards a repair instead of leaving immediately. grandma arranged for a repairer to mend the special pot safely. tom helped pack the pieces and carried the box beside her. afterwards, he moved his bag hook away from the display shelf. grandma put the repaired pot back while he hung his bag carefully.","constructClaim":"theme_vs_plot","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.theme_vs_plot.v3","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.theme_vs_plot.v3","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Tom helped pack the broken teapot before visiting the repairer.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN","A precious object should be replaced as soon as it grows old.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Family stories can make a familiar object feel more special.":"D-TOPIC-ADJACENT"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v4","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Trying a new routine can make a familiar job more exciting."},{"id":"c1","label":"The keeper cleaned the lighthouse glass throughout forty years of service."},{"id":"c2","label":"Useful work can matter deeply even when its worker is unseen."},{"id":"c3","label":"Teaching a skill is the best way to become widely famous."}],"answer":"c2","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v4","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which message does the whole story support?","passage":"For forty years, the lighthouse keeper checked the lamp each night. He cleaned the glass even when nobody visited the little island. Most sailors saw the signal without ever learning his name. He sometimes wondered whether anyone noticed the hours spent maintaining it. At retirement, letters arrived from ships that had followed its light. One sailor described finding the harbour safely during a dark storm. The keeper read the letter beside his neatly stored cleaning tools. He left the tools ready for the person taking his place.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Trying a new routine can make a familiar job more exciting."},{"id":"c1","label":"The keeper cleaned the lighthouse glass throughout forty years of service."},{"id":"c2","label":"Useful work can matter deeply even when its worker is unseen."},{"id":"c3","label":"Teaching a skill is the best way to become widely famous."}],"answer":"c2","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which message does the whole story support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"for forty years, the lighthouse keeper checked the lamp each night. he cleaned the glass even when nobody visited the little island. most sailors saw the signal without ever learning his name. he sometimes wondered whether anyone noticed the hours spent maintaining it. at retirement, letters arrived from ships that had followed its light. one sailor described finding the harbour safely during a dark storm. the keeper read the letter beside his neatly stored cleaning tools. he left the tools ready for the person taking his place.","constructClaim":"theme_vs_plot","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v4","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v4","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Teaching a skill is the best way to become widely famous.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Trying a new routine can make a familiar job more exciting.":"D-TOPIC-ADJACENT","The keeper cleaned the lighthouse glass throughout forty years of service.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_vs_plot.v5","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Making matching decorations can help a group feel united."},{"id":"c1","label":"Following other people’s designs can save useful planning time."},{"id":"c2","label":"Amaya’s small lantern stayed upright during the windy evening parade."},{"id":"c3","label":"A sound design can matter more than an impressive appearance."}],"answer":"c3","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_vs_plot.v5","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which message does the whole story support?","passage":"Amaya planned a lantern for the windy evening parade near the coast. She used a small frame with strong joins and thick covering. Friends chose taller shapes that looked grand beside her plain little lantern. Amaya checked her joins once more instead of adding extra height. Along the route, a gust tore the thin sides of several lanterns. Some large frames bent, and their owners carried them folded home. Amaya''s light stayed covered inside its firm frame throughout the walk. At the finish, she could still hold it upright beside her drawing.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Making matching decorations can help a group feel united."},{"id":"c1","label":"Following other people’s designs can save useful planning time."},{"id":"c2","label":"Amaya’s small lantern stayed upright during the windy evening parade."},{"id":"c3","label":"A sound design can matter more than an impressive appearance."}],"answer":"c3","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which message does the whole story support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"amaya planned a lantern for the windy evening parade near the coast. she used a small frame with strong joins and thick covering. friends chose taller shapes that looked grand beside her plain little lantern. amaya checked her joins once more instead of adding extra height. along the route, a gust tore the thin sides of several lanterns. some large frames bent, and their owners carried them folded home. amaya''s light stayed covered inside its firm frame throughout the walk. at the finish, she could still hold it upright beside her drawing.","constructClaim":"theme_vs_plot","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_vs_plot.v5","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_vs_plot.v5","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Making matching decorations can help a group feel united.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Following other people’s designs can save useful planning time.":"D-TOPIC-ADJACENT","Amaya’s small lantern stayed upright during the windy evening parade.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.theme_vs_plot.v6","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Dividing jobs by existing skills is enough preparation for every task."},{"id":"c1","label":"Working quickly gives other people more time to finish carefully."},{"id":"c2","label":"Tup and Lin helped Priw learn to make strong wooden joins."},{"id":"c3","label":"Avoiding difficulty can mean missing a chance to learn."}],"answer":"c3","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.theme_vs_plot.v6","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which message does the whole story support?","passage":"Priw chose the easiest jobs during the class woodwork project. He carried boards while Tup and Lin practised making strong joins. At first, he enjoyed finishing quickly while they corrected their mistakes. Later, each child needed to build a small frame alone. Priw could measure wood but did not know how to join it. Tup and Lin remembered the problems they had already worked through. Priw asked to practise beside them before starting his frame again. This time, he chose to try the part he had avoided.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Dividing jobs by existing skills is enough preparation for every task."},{"id":"c1","label":"Working quickly gives other people more time to finish carefully."},{"id":"c2","label":"Tup and Lin helped Priw learn to make strong wooden joins."},{"id":"c3","label":"Avoiding difficulty can mean missing a chance to learn."}],"answer":"c3","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which message does the whole story support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"priw chose the easiest jobs during the class woodwork project. he carried boards while tup and lin practised making strong joins. at first, he enjoyed finishing quickly while they corrected their mistakes. later, each child needed to build a small frame alone. priw could measure wood but did not know how to join it. tup and lin remembered the problems they had already worked through. priw asked to practise beside them before starting his frame again. this time, he chose to try the part he had avoided.","constructClaim":"theme_vs_plot","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.theme_vs_plot.v6","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.theme_vs_plot.v6","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Dividing jobs by existing skills is enough preparation for every task.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Working quickly gives other people more time to finish carefully.":"D-TOPIC-ADJACENT","Tup and Lin helped Priw learn to make strong wooden joins.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v7","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Keeping your belongings separate means never helping with others’ things."},{"id":"c1","label":"Winning a reward encourages people to complete routine jobs."},{"id":"c2","label":"Ede stood wet boots apart on the rack in the school drying room."},{"id":"c3","label":"Small thoughtful actions can make a shared place work better."}],"answer":"c3","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v7","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which message does the whole story support?","passage":"Wet boots crowded the school drying room after each rainy walk. Children hurried away, leaving several pairs lying with openings pressed together. Ede noticed that those boots were often still damp after lunch. She began standing the pairs apart on the shared rack. She also showed younger children where to leave space around each pair. By afternoon, more children could put on comfortable dry boots. Nobody had asked Ede to earn points or win a prize. She kept a gap on the rack for the last arriving pair.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Keeping your belongings separate means never helping with others’ things."},{"id":"c1","label":"Winning a reward encourages people to complete routine jobs."},{"id":"c2","label":"Ede stood wet boots apart on the rack in the school drying room."},{"id":"c3","label":"Small thoughtful actions can make a shared place work better."}],"answer":"c3","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which message does the whole story support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"wet boots crowded the school drying room after each rainy walk. children hurried away, leaving several pairs lying with openings pressed together. ede noticed that those boots were often still damp after lunch. she began standing the pairs apart on the shared rack. she also showed younger children where to leave space around each pair. by afternoon, more children could put on comfortable dry boots. nobody had asked ede to earn points or win a prize. she kept a gap on the rack for the last arriving pair.","constructClaim":"theme_vs_plot","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v7","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v7","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"Keeping your belongings separate means never helping with others’ things.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","Winning a reward encourages people to complete routine jobs.":"D-TOPIC-ADJACENT","Ede stood wet boots apart on the rack in the school drying room.":"D-DETAIL-AS-MAIN"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_vs_plot.v8","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"A good solution can protect belongings while preserving a friendship."},{"id":"c1","label":"Ending every disagreement requires doing all activities separately."},{"id":"c2","label":"Sharing a room means giving up every private space and possession."},{"id":"c3","label":"The twins erased their chalk line and kept separate shelves."}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.theme_vs_plot.v8","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which message does the whole story support?","passage":"The twins drew a chalk line across their shared attic room. Each kept books and models on one side after several arguments. For a few days, neither touched anything that belonged to the other. The room was peaceful, but their half-finished model village stayed untouched. Each missed the ideas and stories they used to share. They talked about asking before borrowing instead of staying completely apart. Then they erased the line and finished one village building together. Their separate shelves remained, with a shared workspace between them.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"A good solution can protect belongings while preserving a friendship."},{"id":"c1","label":"Ending every disagreement requires doing all activities separately."},{"id":"c2","label":"Sharing a room means giving up every private space and possession."},{"id":"c3","label":"The twins erased their chalk line and kept separate shelves."}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which message does the whole story support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-U