nswerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-new-situation-shows-the-same-lesson-6869cf72df.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.apply_theme.v1","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which new situation shows the SAME lesson?","passage":"Luca kept losing his balance during one part of the dance. He managed the earlier steps, then always put a foot down. His teacher suggested short practice periods instead of one exhausting afternoon. Each day, Luca held the difficult position for a little longer. He marked his progress, including days when he wobbled again. After several weeks, he could hold the pose throughout the music. The rest of the dance had not become easier by itself. He had spent time on the part that needed repeated work.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"A pupil practises difficult number problems regularly until they become easier."},{"id":"c1","label":"A pupil chooses an easier dance instead of repeating the difficult part."},{"id":"c2","label":"A pupil lends spare shoes to someone who forgot their dance bag."},{"id":"c3","label":"A pupil explains an unfair score to the teacher before prizes are given."}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which new situation shows the SAME lesson?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-new-situation-shows-the-same-lesson-6869cf72df.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-new-situation-shows-the-same-lesson-6869cf72df.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"luca kept losing his balance during one part of the dance. he managed the earlier steps, then always put a foot down. his teacher suggested short practice 