ding","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which new situation shows the SAME lesson?","passage":"Jules borrowed a neighbour''s plant pot for a school display. While carrying it home, he caught its edge against the gate. A crack spread down the side, though it still stood upright. He first placed it where the damaged part faced the wall. Before returning it, he moved it back and told the neighbour. Jules offered his pocket money and helped choose a suitable replacement. The neighbour thanked him for explaining without waiting to be questioned. Jules carried the new pot with both hands on the next visit.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"A rider lends a spare helmet to a friend who has forgotten one."},{"id":"c1","label":"A rider admits scratching a borrowed bicycle and helps arrange its repair."},{"id":"c2","label":"A rider hides a damaged bicycle behind a shed before its owner returns."},{"id":"c3","label":"A rider practises balancing until a difficult corner becomes easy to turn."}],"answer":"c1","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which new situation shows the SAME lesson?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-new-situation-shows-the-same-lesson-6869cf72df.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-new-situation-shows-the-same-lesson-6869cf72df.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"jules borrowed a neighbour''s plant pot for a school display. while carrying it home, he caught its edge against the gate. a crack spread down the side, though it still stood upright. he first placed it where the damaged part faced the wall. before returning it, he moved it back and told the neighbour. jules offered his pocket money and helped choose a suitable replacement. the neighbour thanked him for explaining without waiting to be questioned. jules carried the new pot with both hands on the next visit.","constructClaim":"apply_theme","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.apply_theme.v2","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.B.apply_theme.v2","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"A rider hides a damaged bicycle behind a shed before its owner returns.":"D-TOPIC-ADJACENT","A rider practises balancing until a difficult corner becomes easy to turn.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","A rider lends a spare helmet to a friend who has forgotten one.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.apply_theme.v3","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"A cook shows one measuring step, then lets a beginner complete it."},{"id":"c1","label":"A cook finishes a beginner’s whole dish while the beginner watches silently."},{"id":"c2","label":"A cook shares a finished cake with a neighbour who has no dessert."},{"id":"c3","label":"A cook gives someone easier food to prepare without explaining any steps."}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-new-situation-shows-the-same-lesson-6869cf72df.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.apply_theme.v3","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which new situation shows the SAME lesson?","passage":"Ray watched a younger child struggle with a large picture puzzle. She had pushed several pieces together although their edges did not match. Ray nearly took over so the table could be cleared quickly. Instead, he showed her how to find the straight edge pieces. He joined one corner while she watched, then moved his hands away. The child tried another corner and began building the outer frame. When she asked, Ray gave a hint without choosing the next piece. She completed the middle herself and called her family over to look.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"A cook shows one measuring step, then lets a beginner complete it."},{"id":"c1","label":"A cook finishes a beginner’s whole dish while the beginner watches silently."},{"id":"c2","label":"A cook shares a finished cake with a neighbour who has no dessert."},{"id":"c3","label":"A cook gives someone easier food to prepare without explaining any steps."}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which new situation shows the SAME lesson?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-new-situation-shows-the-same-lesson-6869cf72df.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-new-situation-shows-the-same-lesson-6869cf72df.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"ray watched a younger child struggle with a large picture puzzle. she had pushed several pieces together although their edges did not match. ray nearly took over so the table could be cleared quickly. instead, he showed her how to find the straight edge pieces. he joined one corner while she watched, then moved his hands away. the child tried another corner and began building the outer frame. when she asked, ray gave a hint without choosing the next piece. she completed the middle herself and called her family over to look.","constructClaim":"apply_theme","sourceItemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.apply_theme.v3","sourceFormat":"COMPREHENSION","sourceProvenance":{"generatedBy":"assessment-rebuild-gate","sourceFile":"tools/assessmentRebuild/authoring/theme_higher_comprehension.mjs","wave":"","standardVersion":"v3"},"mediaDecision":{"itemId":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.C.apply_theme.v3","role":"text-only","paths":[],"constructReview":"approved","answerNeutral":"approved-empty-setting"},"distractorRationales":{"A cook shares a finished cake with a neighbour who has no dessert.":"D-PLAUSIBLE-UNSUPPORTED","A cook gives someone easier food to prepare without explaining any steps.":"D-TOPIC-ADJACENT","A cook finishes a beginner’s whole dish while the beginner watches silently.":"D-OPPOSITE"},"requiredImagePaths":[],"mediaReady":true}},{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.apply_theme.v4","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","level":2,"format":"choice","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"A gardener chooses attractive tools so visitors will admire the tidy shed."},{"id":"c1","label":"A caretaker clears slippery steps early without needing public praise each time."},{"id":"c2","label":"A singer rehearses a difficult song to improve before a public concert."},{"id":"c3","label":"A shopper returns extra change after noticing the cashier made a mistake."}],"answer":"c1","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/which-new-situation-shows-the-same-lesson-6869cf72df.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.apply_theme.v4","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which new situation shows the SAME lesson?","passage":"Evi walked along the village path before most neighbours left home. After windy nights, she checked for small branches across the paving. She moved the light ones and told an adult about heavy ones. When the path was clear, she continued to school as usual. Most walkers arrived later and never saw who had checked it. Once, a neighbour noticed