window lit the children’s faces in her photograph."}],"answer":"c0","answerMode":"exact","requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"itemSnapshot":{"id":"lp3.theme_higher_comprehension.l2.A.theme_vs_plot.v20","contentVersion":"literacy-mock-v1","skillId":"theme","domainId":"reading","mapDomainId":"comprehension","level":2,"format":"choice","answerMode":"exact","prompt":"Which message does the whole story support?","passage":"Mika wanted to take the class photograph without accepting any advice. In her first picture, faces disappeared in shadows beside the window. She tried again from the same place and got the same result. A neighbour who enjoyed photography offered to explain the light. Mika finally listened and moved so the window lit the children''s faces. She checked the new picture before asking everyone to smile again. The finished photograph clearly showed each child in the group. Mika wrote the neighbour''s helpful lighting tip beside her own picture notes.","choices":[{"id":"c0","label":"Accepting guidance can improve work you still do yourself."},{"id":"c1","label":"Replacing old equipment is the quickest way to improve a result."},{"id":"c2","label":"Taking charge means completing every part without advice from anyone."},{"id":"c3","label":"Mika moved so the window lit the children’s faces in her photograph."}],"answer":"c0","targetWord":"","renderTargetText":false,"image":"","imageAlt":"","modality":"reading","displayPassageDuringResponse":true,"hideWrittenLabels":false,"tutorialOnly":false,"requiredAudioCues":[{"role":"instruction","text":"Which message does the whole story support?","path":"/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"}],"requiredAudioPaths":["/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-message-does-the-whole-story-support-0b441f133f.mp3"],"stimulusKey":"mika wanted to take the class photograph wi